  {"date": "1991-11-16", "venue": "The Bayou", "city": "Washington", "state": "DC", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Some unusual bass lines from Mike and organ playing by Page create a strong sense of tension in this ripper.", "note": "Mrs. Pizza Shit reference.", "prev": "Bathtub Gin", "next": "You Enjoy Myself", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1991-11-19", "venue": "The Sting", "city": "New Britain", "state": "CT", "gap": 1, "set": "1", "prev": "Sparkle", "next": "Horn", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1991-11-20", "venue": "Campus Club", "city": "Providence", "state": "RI", "gap": 1, "set": "e", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Carl Gerhard on trumpet. &quot;Brother&quot; already has an exotic sound to it. That sentiment is only enhanced with the addition of a trumpet to the mix.", "note": "Carl Gerhard on trumpet.", "prev": "Magilla", "in": ">", "last": 1, "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1991-11-22", "venue": "Sullivan Gymnasium, University of Southern Maine", "city": "Portland", "state": "ME", "gap": 2, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "While it's far less dissonant than most early versions, there is some truly amazing playing by Trey in this one. Fish and Mike are also strong.", "prev": "Sparkle", "next": "Fee", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1991-11-23", "venue": "Alumni Hall", "city": "Barre", "state": "VT", "gap": 1, "set": "1", "prev": "Uncle Pen", "next": "Bouncing Around the Room", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1991-11-30", "venue": "The Capitol Theatre", "city": "Port Chester", "state": "NY", "gap": 2, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "After a gentle, settling &quot;Squirming Coil&quot;, we have something akin to a combination of &quot;Carini&quot; and &quot;46 Days&quot; on steroids, except that this &quot;Brother&quot; was performed 6 years before either of those beasts were hatched.", "prev": "The Squirming Coil", "in": ">", "next": "Paul and Silas", "nb": 1},
